Aim
To evaluate the performance of a cellular network (throughput, delay and packet loss) as the number of users increases, using OMNeT++ (Simu5G) for simulation and Python for result analysis.
Detailed Algorithm
1.  Define the scenario: a multi-cell LTE/5G NR network (reuse the network from Experiment 22) with one server and a variable number of UEs.
2.  Define the parameters: number of UEs (10, 20, 40), UE speed (3 m/s pedestrian), traffic (UDP downlink, 1000 B every 10 ms per UE), simulation time 60 s, 5 repetitions per setting.
3.  Declare a parameter study in omnetpp.ini using iteration variables so that one run command executes all combinations.
4.  Run all simulations in batch mode (Cmdenv) and store the scalar results (.sca files).
5.  Write a Python script that reads the .sca files, groups the values by the number of UEs and averages over the repetitions and UEs.
6.  Compute throughput per UE, mean end-to-end delay and packet loss ratio.
7.  Tabulate and plot the results; interpret how the cell load affects the performance metrics.
8.  Prepare the project report: objective, scenario, parameters, results, discussion and conclusion.
